cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Exactly three theta mates for a family of rank-four lattices"
abstract: >-
  A tensor construction over the Eisenstein integers gives, for every
  positive definite integral binary form M = (a, b, c), three even lattices
  of rank four with the same theta series, pairwise non-isometric for
  generic M (0 < 2b < a < c). This release proves that for every generic
  integer seed, with no bound and no residue condition, every positive
  definite rank-four lattice with that theta series is isometric to exactly
  one of the three. The proof is computer-assisted: hand reductions accepted
  in AI-assisted review (not peer review), combined with exact certificates, exact isometry tests and
  complete finite searches, every one re-executed in complete runs of record
  from one frozen evidence archive (sha256
  ba42fe97adb4202a445d60f34d5b47d5c632ecc4f770790cb911acfc53ba572f). It
  concerns this constructed family only and gives no upper bound for
  rank-four theta fibres in general. No literature-priority claim is made.
authors:
  - name: "bigjokker"
type: software
license: MIT
